Part 1 — Understand the Business Problem — 10 Points
Answer:
What is the business problem?
The business problem is data science job salaries. Organization is hiring for data science roles often struggle to determine the fair and competitive salaries. Compensation varies widely by work year, experience level, employment type, job title, salary, remote ratio, etc. Without reliable benchmarking data, HR teams and hiring managers may set salaries based on guesswork or outdated information rather than current market trends. This can cause organization to overpay for unecessarily or underpay compared to competitors, risking either wasted budget or loss of talent. 
Why is this problem important to the organization?
This problem is important to the organization because it help organization to attract and keep good data science talent. If pay is too low, employees may leave for better offers, and organization struggles to fill important role. If pay is too high, it wastes budget and reduce profit, especially when hiring more people in the same role. This problem also affects trust within the organization, because employees expect fair pay compare to others doing similar role.
Who is affected by this problem?
- HR teams
- Hiring Managers
- Current Employees
- Job Seekers
